<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="5">
<Content>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. ALDRIDGE DRY GOODS BUILDING - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Through a facepiece. The edges of the lens frame everything. Breathing, close, already going.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Gloved hands come up on both sides of the lens and press. A thumb runs the seal. Behind the hands, masked, CAPTAIN CARL SLOAN, 50s, barrel-chested, gray mustache. The man inside the facepiece is DANNY MERCER, 25, probationary firefighter, broad-shouldered, young.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SLOAN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(muffled, mask)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Air?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MERCER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(muffled, mask)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Full.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Sloan puts the regulator to the mask and it clicks home. He takes Mercer&#x27;s shoulder strap in his fist and turns him toward the building.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A two-story red-brick building on a block of shuttered storefronts. Smoke pulses from the eaves. No flame visible. An ENGINE at the corner, EARL DOBBS, 40s, company engineer, at the pump panel looking up at the roofline. Ladders going to the roof. The RIT team waiting with tools.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>At the command board, the INCIDENT COMMANDER, radio traffic in both ears.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(into radio)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Command to all units, building reported vacant, occupancy unconfirmed. Engine Three, you&#x27;re interior. Give me conditions when you&#x27;ve got them.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Sloan&#x27;s hand comes off the strap long enough to point at the hose. The door. The dark past it. They get low and go in.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. ALDRIDGE DRY GOODS BUILDING - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>BLACK.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Breathing. Close, mechanical, air pulled through a regulator, pushed back out.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Water moving. A pump throbbing far off, through walls.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A helmet lamp comes up: light that reaches three feet.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Gloved hands on a hoseline, following it forward. The line is the only road in here. Back along it is the door.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The lamp finds the nozzle. Mercer braces behind it. Sloan keeps one hand on his shoulder strap.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>They move on their hands and knees. Heat keeps them there.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SLOAN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(muffled, mask)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Pencil it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Mercer opens the nozzle at the overhead, one short burst. It comes back down on them as hissing steam. They keep moving.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MERCER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Where is it?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SLOAN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Above us or ahead of us. Watch your ceiling.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Sloan keys the radio on his chest.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SLOAN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(radio)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Heavy smoke. High heat. Zero visibility. We&#x27;re penciling.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(radio, tinny)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Interior, you in position with a charged line?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SLOAN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(radio)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Charged and on it. It&#x27;s above us. Give us a hole and we&#x27;ll take it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. ALDRIDGE DRY GOODS BUILDING - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Three firefighters sound the roof ahead of every step with pike poles.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(into radio)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Roof, Command. Open it up.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. ALDRIDGE - ROOF - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The saw starts on the third pull. It revs to full power. The blade bites hard into the roof.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Smoke presses along the cut.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The opening breaks through. Smoke stands up in a hard column.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. ALDRIDGE - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The smoke LIFTS a foot off the floor.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The building appears as the draft takes hold: shelving rows. A dead forklift. An aisle. For the first time, a shape to the dark.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SLOAN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>There&#x27;s our vent. Move.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>They advance up the aisle, the line paying out behind them.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Outside, the engine pump climbs higher, Dobbs feeding them more pressure.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Ahead, the ceiling GLOWS through its seams.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Fire rolls from the ceiling void, across the overhead, running for the vent. Above the roof the cut throws flame, and the roof crew goes flat.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Behind Sloan, a section of ceiling and steel rack lets go. CRASHES across the hoseline.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The lamp beams disappear into black.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SLOAN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Back it out! Back --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The hose line is pinned beneath the debris. Sloan hauls at it. Mercer is three feet deeper into the room, cut off from Sloan by burning shelving. Three feet.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>MERCER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Cap --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The VIBRALERT goes off against his jaw. Low air.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SLOAN</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(radio)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>MAYDAY MAYDAY MAYDAY. Engine Three. Firefighter separated. Northeast corner. Low air --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(radio, tinny, far)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Command copies the Mayday. RIT is deploying.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Mercer, alone.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He drops a glove onto the hoseline and follows it. The line goes two ways. One way is the nozzle. The other is the door.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Five feet. A coupling. His fingers find the lugs on the far side. Lugs point to the nozzle. Wrong way. He has been crawling deeper in. He turns and crawls back along the line.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The regulator gives him less air. The Vibralert pounds, slows, then stops. He inhales and gets nothing; the facepiece seal pulls tight against his cheeks.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>His gloves grip the edges of the facepiece.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He does not pull it off. He releases it and puts both hands back on the hoseline.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He crawls. Slower now. Each attempt to inhale pulls the seal tighter. His helmet light drops toward the floor.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He stops moving.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The beam remains fixed across the floor. Smoke passes through it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>His PASS device begins to chirp. The warning accelerates, then rises into a full electronic SHRIEK.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Nothing else moves. Faint traffic comes through the radio on his chest:</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SLOAN (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(radio, tinny)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Mercer. Mercer, key your mic.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Nothing. The shriek. Smoke crossing the beam.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>RIT OFFICER (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(radio)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>RIT to Command, we&#x27;re at the collapse. No contact. We&#x27;re digging.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(radio)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Command to all units, emergency traffic only. Three minutes on the Mayday.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The beam is dimmer. The smoke is thick and rolling.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>SLOAN (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(radio, raw)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>He was right beside me. He&#x27;s on the line. He is ON the line --</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>INCIDENT COMMANDER (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(radio)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>RIT, Command. Status.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Static. No answer.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>The beam. The smoke. The shriek.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A GLOVED HAND reaches through the smoke, finds Mercer&#x27;s shoulder strap and locks on.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>RIT FIREFIGHTER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(muffled, close)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>GOT HIM! We got him! GO!</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Mercer is YANKED backward. Floorboards rush beneath him. His lamp swings away from the beam.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. ALDRIDGE - ENTRY DOOR - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Two RIT firefighters drag Mercer across the threshold. His mask is still sealed. His PASS continues to scream until one of them shuts it off.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Clean air. Concrete apron. Mask off. Helmet off.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>A FIREFIGHTER-MEDIC&#x27;s fingers go to his throat.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>FIREFIGHTER-MEDIC</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>No pulse. Starting compressions.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Coat open. Compressions. Bag-valve mask. AED pads. Behind them, the building ROARS as master streams open up.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Mercer COUGHS, wet, tearing. Fights the mask on his face.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>FIREFIGHTER-MEDIC</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Pulse. We got a pulse. Package him.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He keys the mic on his shoulder.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>FIREFIGHTER-MEDIC</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Command, Medical. I want the helicopter.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>COMMAND (V.O.)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Say again, Medical.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>FIREFIGHTER-MEDIC</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Helicopter. He was down and he&#x27;s back. We need to get him to the nearest trauma center.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. ALDRIDGE - CLEARING - LATER</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Open ground a hundred yards off the fire. The aircraft comes up off the grass with Mercer inside it. Rotor wash drives ash flat across the lot. The firefighters under it turn their backs.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>It noses over the tree line. Gone.</Text></Paragraph>
</Content>
</FinalDraft>
